 "proof": [
  {
   "text": "The opens $U$ and $X_i\\setminus\\overline Z_{i,j}$ cover $W_i$. The first\nis separated and of finite type over $S$ by the section hypotheses. The\nsecond has those properties because it is open in the proper scheme\n$X_i\\to S$. Their overlap map is the closed immersion supplied by\n[lemma-nagata-intermediate-overlap-closed]. Apply\n[lemma-nagata-separated-two-open-cover] to these two opens to obtain\nseparatedness of $W_i\\to S$. Finite type is local on this finite open\ncover, so $W_i\\to S$ is also of finite type.",
   "uses": [
    "lemma-nagata-intermediate-overlap-closed",
    "lemma-nagata-separated-two-open-cover"
   ],
   "elementary": false
  }
 ],
